00:12:53.917 --> 00:12:56.500
and then you
basically have this ecosystem

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.625
of a lot of talented
engineers and product people

00:12:58.625 --> 00:12:59.542
that are teaming up.

00:12:59.542 --> 00:13:00.959
It's just a talent game,

00:13:00.959 --> 00:13:03.291
and it's very easy to
move within the U.S. from,

00:13:03.291 --> 00:13:04.208
to San Francisco.

00:13:04.208 --> 00:13:06.458
So the talent,
I actually think plays out.

00:13:06.458 --> 00:13:07.834
I think entrepreneurship

00:13:07.834 --> 00:13:11.333
is inherently rewarded
in the United States,

00:13:11.333 --> 00:13:13.875
while it's still
historically in Europe,

00:13:13.875 --> 00:13:15.500
it's finally chipping away,

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:16.750
it's why I'm so
happy to be here.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.208
But historically,
failing in America,

00:13:19.208 --> 00:13:21.667
though tough,
is not a deathblow.

00:13:21.667 --> 00:13:24.583
Failing in Europe
is a scarlet letter.

00:13:24.583 --> 00:13:28.834
And that has been the death
of entrepreneurship over time,

00:13:28.834 --> 00:13:31.834
in Europe.

00:13:31.834 --> 00:13:34.542
I think that
there's infrastructure

00:13:34.542 --> 00:13:36.792
in history of consumer behavior.

00:13:36.792 --> 00:13:38.667
The internet is just,

00:13:38.667 --> 00:13:40.458
though you see
interesting things,

00:13:40.458 --> 00:13:42.917
like the U.K. market has a
healthier e-commerce business

00:13:42.917 --> 00:13:45.083
than the U.S.
market in a lot of ways.

00:13:45.083 --> 00:13:47.000
But I think a
couple of those factors,

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.417
Venture Capital
money is consolidated,

00:13:49.417 --> 00:13:50.792
which is giving a lot of people

00:13:50.792 --> 00:13:52.208
the ability to build businesses

00:13:52.208 --> 00:13:53.500
that don't have
to be profitable,

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:54.583
and have been
able to get through

00:13:54.583 --> 00:13:55.875
and build very big businesses.

00:13:55.875 --> 00:13:57.959
And the
infrastructure of communication.

00:13:57.959 --> 00:14:00.375
The biggest
websites in the world,

00:14:00.375 --> 00:14:02.291
the far majority of
them outside of China,

00:14:02.291 --> 00:14:04.667
East-based companies
are based in the U.S.,

00:14:04.667 --> 00:14:06.333
and China is a closed door.

00:14:06.333 --> 00:14:07.750
So nobody's
really doing much there.

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:09.041
It's insular nationalism.

00:14:09.041 --> 00:14:10.625
Whereas a lot of
people are doing it.

00:14:10.625 --> 00:14:12.708
Now, that being said,

00:14:12.708 --> 00:14:16.166
Spotify, SoundCloud,
there's amazing accomplishments

00:14:16.166 --> 00:14:18.250
that have worked over there.

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.458
But I think
you're going so macro,

00:14:20.458 --> 00:14:21.875
I'm way more
concerned about the micro.

00:14:21.875 --> 00:14:25.083
I think you can't focus,
or be crippled by that,

00:14:25.083 --> 00:14:27.166
you just need focus on even
being able to win that game,

00:14:27.166 --> 00:14:29.792
if that's your ambition.
You know?

00:14:29.792 --> 00:14:30.625
The good news is,

00:14:30.625 --> 00:14:32.041
if you win that game,

00:14:32.041 --> 00:14:33.667
that means that
you've raised a lot of money

00:14:33.667 --> 00:14:35.375
from a lot of
very important people,

00:14:35.375 --> 00:14:38.125
who will deploy that
political and financial capital

00:14:38.125 --> 00:14:40.208
against you staying alive.

00:14:40.208 --> 00:14:41.208
To win in the U.S.,

00:14:41.208 --> 00:14:42.667
you've built a
billion dollar company.

00:14:42.667 --> 00:14:43.542
Unless you're looking

00:14:43.542 --> 00:14:45.041
to build a very
practical small business,

00:14:45.041 --> 00:14:47.458
and then I would
diversify, period.

00:14:47.458 --> 00:14:49.458
Then you don't
need the U.S. necessarily.

00:14:49.458 --> 00:14:50.959
Do you know what I mean?

00:14:50.959 --> 00:14:52.625
You need the US if
you're going global

00:14:52.625 --> 00:14:53.959
and building a
billion dollar company.

00:14:53.959 --> 00:14:55.500
You don't need
the U.S. to build a 10,

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:59.917
or even $100 million business.

00:14:59.917 --> 00:15:00.750
You got it.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:01.583
Hey, man.

00:15:01.583 --> 00:15:02.792
- [Dries] I'm
Dries from LifePower.

00:15:02.792 --> 00:15:03.625
- How are you?

00:15:03.625 --> 00:15:04.750
- [Dries] Good, good, thanks.
- Good.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.500
- [Dries] We're building a next
generation of power products

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:10.125
