00:15:17.166 --> 00:15:19.583
how do you decide
whether or not to go

00:15:19.583 --> 00:15:22.542
for a business opportunity
when it presents itself?

00:15:22.542 --> 00:15:25.458
For example,
a customer pops up and says,

00:15:25.458 --> 00:15:27.667
"Hey, but can't you
do this custom for us?"

00:15:27.667 --> 00:15:29.792
and we're like, "That
could be possible, but--"

00:15:29.792 --> 00:15:31.667
- But it takes away
from our core mission.

00:15:31.667 --> 00:15:32.875
- [Dries] Exactly.
- So classic.

00:15:32.875 --> 00:15:34.125
- [Dries] Exactly.

00:15:34.125 --> 00:15:36.291
It's a go or no go strategy.

00:15:36.291 --> 00:15:40.041
- That is gonna be
predicated on how good you are.

00:15:40.041 --> 00:15:41.041
- [Dries] Okay.

00:15:41.041 --> 00:15:42.625
- Those are decisions
I can't make for you.

00:15:42.625 --> 00:15:43.792
There's not tried-and-true.

00:15:43.792 --> 00:15:46.583
There's been plenty of
people who did a side project,

00:15:46.583 --> 00:15:48.834
customized, which did two
things: gave them the money

00:15:48.834 --> 00:15:50.750
to stay alive and
showed them something

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:51.834
they never thought of

00:15:51.834 --> 00:15:53.500
which then built
their biggest product.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.333
Then, there's been
companies that got distracted

00:15:55.333 --> 00:15:57.417
and became an agency in
the client service business

00:15:57.417 --> 00:15:58.583
and missed their opportunity.

00:15:58.583 --> 00:16:01.041
Both have
happened a trillion times.

00:16:01.041 --> 00:16:03.708
No guy from the U.S.
who's been successful

00:16:03.708 --> 00:16:05.458
is gonna tell
you the right answer.

00:16:05.458 --> 00:16:06.667
You're gonna make those calls

00:16:06.667 --> 00:16:08.875
and your success is
gonna be predicated on it.

00:16:08.875 --> 00:16:10.583
You know what the
best part about that is?

00:16:10.583 --> 00:16:12.083
That's the way it should be.

00:16:12.083 --> 00:16:15.959
That's what capitalism
and meritocracy is.

00:16:15.959 --> 00:16:17.000
How good are you?

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:17.959
Did you make the right call?

00:16:17.959 --> 00:16:19.458
'Cause they're both right,

00:16:19.458 --> 00:16:21.625
but they're not
both right for you.

00:16:21.625 --> 00:16:24.708
Question is will you make the
right call when it matters?

00:16:24.708 --> 00:16:26.417
- [Dries] We'll see.
- We'll see.

00:16:26.417 --> 00:16:27.166
But that's the answer.

00:16:27.166 --> 00:16:30.083
Don't be crippled by it and
more importantly, don't--

00:16:30.083 --> 00:16:30.917
(laughing)

00:16:30.917 --> 00:16:33.458
- [Dries] Fast, make that
decision really, really fast.

00:16:33.458 --> 00:16:34.125
- [Man] Flip coin.

00:16:34.125 --> 00:16:37.250
- They're literally
potentially both right.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:38.959
If it doesn't
come to you right away,

00:16:38.959 --> 00:16:40.125
it's only gonna get harder.

00:16:40.125 --> 00:16:42.959
The more you sit on something,
it gets harder, not easier.

00:16:42.959 --> 00:16:43.667
- [Dries] True.

00:16:43.667 --> 00:16:46.041
- People think like
they're gonna figure it out.

00:16:46.041 --> 00:16:48.291
They're gonna figure
it out by tasting it.

00:16:48.291 --> 00:16:49.458
Should I eat this cherry?

00:16:49.458 --> 00:16:50.917
Will I like it?

00:16:52.625 --> 00:16:55.792
The right strategy is
to fuckin' eat the cherry.

00:16:55.792 --> 00:16:57.000
Right?

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.583
Then you'll know.

00:16:58.583 --> 00:17:01.291
Truth is, you
should probably do both.

00:17:01.291 --> 00:17:02.500
- [Dries] If we can, 
but if we can't.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:03.500
- If you can.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:04.583
- [Dries] That
works a couple of times,

00:17:04.583 --> 00:17:06.916
but if a tenth person
is ringing at your door,

00:17:06.916 --> 00:17:08.083
it's like, oh.

00:17:08.083 --> 00:17:10.125
- Yeah, but then if the tenth
person's ringing at your door,

00:17:10.125 --> 00:17:11.040
you need to
figure out why the fuck

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:12.791
they're ringing at your door.

00:17:12.791 --> 00:17:15.165
Maybe the right move is
to actually build a business

00:17:15.165 --> 00:17:17.083
that does do that
and is highly profitable

00:17:17.083 --> 00:17:20.083
so that you have cash
when the world dries up of cash

00:17:20.083 --> 00:17:22.000
and you're not at the
mercy of VCs and raising money,

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.791
but you actually made
cash 'cause you were an agency

00:17:23.791 --> 00:17:26.750
for four years and then you're
37Signals and Jason Fried

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.500
which is they were an
agency and they converted

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:32.000
into their product and
they became a huge business.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.750
People are fancy.

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:37.375
People when they have
nothing say dumb shit like,

00:17:37.375 --> 00:17:39.792
"Yes, but the economics are
in building our own product,

00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:41.417
"not in services."

00:17:41.417 --> 00:17:43.417
You don't have anything.

00:17:44.917 --> 00:17:45.834
- [Dries] Yet.

00:17:45.834 --> 00:17:46.875
- Yet.

00:17:46.875 --> 00:17:49.208
But the best way to
have something is actually

00:17:49.208 --> 00:17:52.500
do something
that's bringing you money.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.834
- [Dries] Good choice.

00:17:53.834 --> 00:17:54.917
- I think so.

00:17:56.375 --> 00:17:58.041
- [Josef] Hi, Gary.
- Hey.

