that he was worth trusting

00:18:33.375 --> 00:18:36.750
and now Patrick
and Ryan and Travis.

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:38.667
Everybody's trying to scale.

00:18:38.667 --> 00:18:42.959
Scaling the unscalable is how
you get to the point of scale,

00:18:42.959 --> 00:18:46.375
so either your number
two has got Belgium on lock

00:18:46.375 --> 00:18:48.166
and you can go to Paris

00:18:48.166 --> 00:18:52.041
or she or he can go to Paris,

00:18:52.041 --> 00:18:55.959
but don't hire
somebody on a whim

00:18:55.959 --> 00:18:58.000
because you don't know
what you're dealing with

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.625
and then you lose.

00:18:59.625 --> 00:19:00.708
Or you can win.

00:19:00.708 --> 00:19:01.667
- [Josef] Yeah, yeah.

00:19:01.667 --> 00:19:02.834
- But you're risking it.

00:19:02.834 --> 00:19:05.875
I don't think opening a
new market is worth risk

00:19:05.875 --> 00:19:09.500
'cause it can take you down.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.834
So what I like
to do is over hire.

00:19:11.834 --> 00:19:14.583
I would probably hire
an extra person or two here

00:19:14.583 --> 00:19:17.333
